    "text": "To solve for \\( f(3) \\) given the functional equation \\( xf(y) = yf(x) \\) and the condition \\( f(15) = 20 \\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Substitute \\( x = 15 \\) and \\( y = 3 \\) into the functional equation:**\n   \\[\n   15f(3) = 3f(15)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Substitute the given value \\( f(15) = 20 \\) into the equation:**\n   \\[\n   15f(3) = 3 \\cdot 20\n   \\]\n\n3. **Simplify the right-hand side:**\n   \\[\n   15f(3) = 60\n   \\]\n\n4. **Solve for \\( f(3) \\) by dividing both sides by 15:**\n   \\[\n   f(3) = \\frac{60}{15}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the final value:**\n   \\[\n   f(3) = 4\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( f(3) \\) is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).",
